{
  "protocol": {
    "request": "<client_id>|<json>",
    "reply": "PIME_MSG|<client_id>|<json>",
    "prefix": "PIME_MSG",
    "separator": "|",
    "maxsplit": 1,
    "echoesSeqNum": true
  },
  "clientId": "12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789abc",
  "guid": {
    "python": "{C5F37DA0-274E-4837-9B7C-9BB79FE85D9D}",
    "node": "{C5F37DA0-274E-4837-9B7C-9BB79FE85D9D}",
    "go": "{7A1C2E93-5B64-4F88-AE21-3D9C6B70F145}",
    "rust": "{C5F37DA0-274E-4837-9B7C-9BB79FE85D9D}"
  },
  "unknownGuid": "{00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000}",
  "replyKeys": [
    "success",
    "seqNum",
    "return",
    "compositionString",
    "compositionCursor",
    "commitString",
    "candidateList",
    "candidateCursor",
    "showCandidates",
    "setSelKeys",
    "openKeyboard",
    "customizeUI",
    "addButton",
    "removeButton",
    "changeButton",
    "addPreservedKey",
    "removePreservedKey",
    "showMessage",
    "hideMessage"
  ],
  "uiKeys": [
    "candFontName",
    "candFontSize",
    "candFontWeight",
    "candPerRow",
    "candUseCursor",
    "candTextColor",
    "windowBackgroundColor",
    "selKeyColor"
  ],
  "buttonKeys": [
    "id",
    "icon",
    "text",
    "tooltip",
    "commandId",
    "type",
    "enable",
    "toggled"
  ],
  "preservedKeyKeys": [
    "keyCode",
    "modifiers",
    "guid"
  ],
  "messageKeys": [
    "message",
    "duration"
  ],
  "extraKeys": [
    "error",
    "cursorPos",
    "selStart",
    "selEnd"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "One case is one session: a fresh client id, the listed steps in order, one reply line per step that carries one.",
    "A step's reply is the SUBSET every adapter must answer; an adapter may add keys, and each suite asserts every key it emits is listed in replyKeys or extraKeys (nested maps use uiKeys, buttonKeys, preservedKeyKeys, messageKeys).",
    "reply null means the frame produces no reply line at all.",
    "The string '$guid' is replaced by guid[<adapter>]; '$unknownGuid' by unknownGuid. Each backend ships its own ime.json, so the registered guid differs per adapter (docs/adr/0004-per-backend-profile-guids.md); the launcher is a pass-through and reuses the python twin's value.",
    "The 'return' key answers the TSF eaten/not-eaten question: python and node write JSON booleans, go writes 1/0, so a harness compares it with true folded to 1 and false to 0.",
    "Where two adapters genuinely disagree, only the keys they share appear in the reply: go answers onCompartmentChanged and onKeyboardStatusChanged with its unknown-method branch, and node drops a seqNum that was absent from the request.",
    "The go backend's Response struct also writes cursorPos, selStart and selEnd, which no PIMEClient.cpp reader consumes; they sit in extraKeys so a suite can still check every emitted key against this file."
  ],
